{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "ecc715a2-4339-56c5-9d11-1fad0ce39817",
  "Description": "300 balls rain on the bunny loaded from a .vdb file.\n\n[LoadVdb] reads the level set, [VolumeResample] makes it coarse enough to collide with, and [VolumeToMesh] turns it into geometry. That geometry goes to a static [RigidBody] as the collider and to [GeometryToMesh] to be drawn, so what the balls hit is what you see.\n\nAKA: openvdb, vdb collider, level set, houdini, bunny, mesh collider\n\nTips\n- VoxelSize on [VolumeResample] sets the cost: at the file's own 0.05 the bunny is 2.7 million triangles, at 0.5 about 45 thousand.\n- The volume is meshed once, when it loads. A volume that changes every frame would rebuild the collider every frame.\n- The bunny is about 30 units tall, which is why the balls and the camera distance are large.",
